   },
   "id": "2102860599281529295",
   "url": "https://x.com/txsportsdoc/status/2102860599281529295",
   "conversationId": "2102752823158907108",
   "text": "💯 in my area of North Texas. If you use some anchors and a patch, without carve outs your negative. Not a good biz model. I personally think there is little to no benefit from these and is another industry generated product that created a product for a problem that didnt exist. There may be a few indications ie focal mid substance tear, of course can always sew side to side with inexpensive suture. I’m Chief at our facility so I am the one who sees it all",
   "lang": "en",
   "createdAt": "2026-09-23T20:40:10.000Z",
   "type": "reply",
   "author": {
    "id": "91464818",
    "username": "txsportsdoc",
    "name": "Robert Berry, DO",
