   "url": "https://x.com/txsportsdoc/status/2102811861817131304",
   "conversationId": "2102752823158907108",
   "text": "You proved my point with this paper and what I have seen practically. Industry is all over promoting these things. I don’t know a single Orthopedic Surgeon putting these in, that doesn’t have some sort of financial benefit. I also see a lot of these in second opinion with Tatian, or reactions that wants them out. Completing a partial tear and adding a couple lateral anchors takes me a couple minutes at most. Maybe large hospital systems have carve out based on certain insurance plans, but most Surgery centers don’t have carve outs for these which means if you have someone using a lot of these, they are losing money every single case.",
   "lang": "en",
