   "url": "https://x.com/txsportsdoc/status/2102774683846279245",
   "conversationId": "2102490008246690149",
   "text": "Disagree. Patients can choose to be healthy or not. Yes, some individuals may have genetic predispositions to certain illnesses, we can create a separate risk pool and fund that and keep them out of the general pool. This would be a good use of government subsidies and lower the cost of health ins premiums exponentially. Median American spend on healthcare annually is less than $500. If that’s the case, why make people spend multiples more for “coverage” makes zero sense.",
