   "url": "https://x.com/txsportsdoc/status/2102766760332063000",
   "conversationId": "2102766760332063000",
   "text": "Hey @SaraGonzalesTX and @BreannaMorello love to see you cover what’s happening in Celina,TX. Armed police officers banging on doors, issuing water violation tickets for watering. The city keeps building and issuing more building permits but doesn’t have enough water for its current residents. No surrounding cities are on such restrictions.  Celina is contracted to purchase 10.5 million gallons from Upper Trinity Regional Water District per day but using 12.1 million at peak. There are now approx 20,142 meters in 2026 vs 16,865 in 2024. The City of Celina Water Contract was entered into in 2020 for 1M gallons/day. https://interchange.puc.texas.gov/Documents/49225_91_1063471.PDF?utm_source=chatgpt.com\nIn 2025 the city requested 10.5 gallons/day but is proving not to be enough. Instead of solving the problem: Limiting growth until a solution is reached, we have now resorted to using armed police officers to issue tickets to citizens. Seems previous Celina Mayor, who was a real estate developer, did what many local mayors have done, committed their cities to rapid growth/development. Unfortunately it seems, the city of Celina didn’t plan for this growth.",
   "lang": "en",
   "createdAt": "2026-09-23T14:27:17.000Z",
