   "url": "https://x.com/txsportsdoc/status/2102763312941334710",
   "conversationId": "2102752823158907108",
   "text": "That’s a rotator cuff tear code. The 22 modifier is used to identify a more difficult and challenging case which is almost a guarantee not to get the 29827 paid. Most of us do not even bill the 22 modifier anymore, because unless you have a solid billing department who follows up on this, it will be denied, and then written off, and the surgeon may not even know it.\n\nUnless you are working at a facility that has implant carve outs that amount of money will come off the top from the reimbursement and often result in a  net loss for the facility.",
   "lang": "en",
